/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (A growing body of evidence demonstrates a direct link between diversity and financial performance in the financial sector. Studies by McKinsey & Company and others consistently show that companies with more diverse leadership teams and workforces outperform their less diverse counterparts. For example, companies in the top quartile for racial and ethnic diversity are 30% more likely to have above-average financial returns, while those in the top quartile for gender diversity see a 15% increase in profitability. This positive correlation holds true across various metrics, including earnings before interest and taxes \(EBIT\), return on investment \(ROI\), and market share.)
/E (A growing body of evidence demonstrates a direct link between diversity and financial performance in the financial sector. Studies by McKinsey & Company and others consistently show that companies with more diverse leadership teams and workforces outperform their less diverse counterparts. For example, companies in the top quartile for racial and ethnic diversity are 30% more likely to have above-average financial returns, while those in the top quartile for gender diversity see a 15% increase in profitability. This positive correlation holds true across various metrics, including earnings before interest and taxes \(EBIT\), return on investment \(ROI\), and market share.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
